From 74c642daedb19f1ad2fd1d67176c2a21fb354fba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:05:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: add kitty text composition

Add an opt-in text composition strategy that preserves grayscale glyph coverage and blends foreground and background colors in linear sRGB. Keep the existing encoded-RGB path as the default.
---
 dist/monstar.5       | 10 +++++
 src/App.zig          |  4 ++
 src/AsyncRaster.zig  | 13 +++++-
 src/Config.zig       | 12 ++++++
 src/Renderer.zig     |  8 ++++
 src/pixel_raster.zig | 98 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 6 files changed, 138 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/monstar.5 b/dist/monstar.5
index bbff5ed..f47f45c 100644
--- a/dist/monstar.5
+++ b/dist/monstar.5
@@ -143,6 +143,16 @@ The result is at least one pixel, and glyphs remain vertically centered.
 Pixel adjustments stay fixed while zooming or changing output scale;
 percentage adjustments follow the font metrics.
 By default no adjustment is applied.
+.TP
+.BI text-composition-strategy " = strategy"
+Set the color composition method for grayscale glyphs.
+.B default
+blends encoded RGB values.
+.B kitty
+decodes sRGB colors, blends them in linear RGB with the original glyph
+coverage, and encodes the result as sRGB.
+The default is
+.BR default .
 .SH WINDOW SETTINGS
 .TP
 .BI background-opacity " = opacity"
